Now , lets rectify the problems we were fcing earlier
adding a server and
removing a server

1.Adding a server :

lets say i add a new server b/w amm s1 and s2 so values b/w s1 and s2 only will get affected others will remain intact.

so only a set of keys which needs to be re-mapped

2.Remove a server :
if we remove some server so again only the conected server will get the load of it but others remain intact


Now, there are still 2 issues :

1.There will be 'non-uniformity' in the key distribution
2.Partition size of data distribution

so we try to minimize these partitions size , the gap b/w like s1 and s2

-either by placing more servers - but this will be costly
so we will palce some virtual servers

so the more partition we do, the data distribution will become more even. 

Hence thats why we introduced the concept of 'Virtual Nodes'

so along with the main servers we place virtual nodes which are having the information of data partition of each server.

so which partition of keys each server is having is kept by these virtual nodes.

so we can look for a key to the nearest server.


Benefits of consistent hashing:
-minimum key redistribution
-easy to scale horizontally
-hotspotting is mitigated










